question:
In a slightly larger Number Wall, add the numbers next to each other and write the sum in the block directly above the two numbers. What number will be in the block labeled '$x$'? Consider the following structure:
[asy]
draw((0,0)--(10,0)--(10,2)--(0,2)--cycle);
draw((2,0)--(2,2));
draw((4,0)--(4,2));
draw((6,0)--(6,2));
draw((8,0)--(8,2));
draw((1,2)--(9,2)--(9,4)--(1,4)--cycle);
draw((3,2)--(3,4));
draw((5,2)--(5,4));
draw((7,2)--(7,4));
draw((2,4)--(2,6)--(8,6)--(8,4)--cycle);
draw((4,4)--(4,6));
draw((6,4)--(6,6));
draw((3,6)--(3,8)--(7,8)--(7,6));
label("$x$",(1,1));
label("5",(3,1));
label("10",(5,1));
label("9",(7,1));
label("6",(9,1));
label("18",(8,3));
label("72",(5,7));
[/asy]
